WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.880
- [Interviewer] So Scott, Scott.

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:07.800
Oh, where'd you grow up?

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.590
Where are you from originally?

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:11.310
- [Scott] I'm originally from Maine.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:15.270
It's where I wished I would have been

00:00:15.270 --> 00:00:16.370
able to grow up.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:17.530
My father was an air force

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:21.113
so we traveled overseas
mostly when I was a kid.

00:00:23.108 --> 00:00:25.130
- [Interviewer] What kind
of childhood did you have?

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:28.610
- It was great until my
dad had to leave to Korea.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.023
He was in the air force,

00:00:31.597 --> 00:00:33.820
you know, career.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.750
And my mom divorced him

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:39.157
in the Midwest and I was not having that.

00:00:39.157 --> 00:00:40.460
You know.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:44.680
I mean, especially living
overseas, like the Philippines.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:49.680
I like adventure and
Nebraska was not adventurous.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:54.090
So I left, I got in trouble
when I was 12 and just left

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:59.593
but it was more or less,
my mom wanted me to go.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.480
It wasn't like I was ended up

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:06.100
on the streets because
of choice, but because of

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:09.010
rejection

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:13.180
- [Interviewer] What kind of
trouble are you getting into?

00:01:13.180 --> 00:01:14.620
- Really nothing illegal.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:16.700
I just wasn't going to school.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.190
I couldn't read or write

00:01:18.190 --> 00:01:21.330
at the time would do math
or any of that stuff.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:22.163
It was nothing.

00:01:22.163 --> 00:01:24.860
The only thing that I
could had any contact

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.020
with were animals.

00:01:27.020 --> 00:01:28.950
And that was strange to my family.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:29.783
So;

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:34.210
well with my mother and brother, my sister

00:01:34.210 --> 00:01:38.710
who was doing good there from
another dad, which makes them

00:01:38.710 --> 00:01:42.830
you know, fortunate because
the dad, I have had problems

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:46.360
and It carried onto me
and it bothered me a lot.

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:51.160
And I wanted to hide that
and running away was my way

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.050
of

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:52.920
hiding

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:54.855
what I really am,

00:01:54.855 --> 00:01:56.030
you know?

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:59.250
And it hurt, you know, I
didn't want people to know.

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:00.710
I couldn't learn.

00:02:00.710 --> 00:02:01.543
And,

00:02:02.540 --> 00:02:03.373
but

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.287
I was 12.

00:02:06.287 --> 00:02:08.181
That was in seventy six.

00:02:08.181 --> 00:02:09.140
- [Interviewer] You ran away at 12.

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:10.350
- Yeah.

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.640
- [Interviewer] So how
far did you get in school?

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.363
- I didn't have a grade,
I was in special ed.

00:02:16.250 --> 00:02:17.820
Yeah, I literally couldn't read

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.740
or write until I was 17, at least.

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.120
And it was hitchhiking

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:26.000
to different cities and States
and seeing this, you know.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:29.083
Welcome to the state of
California that it just caught.

00:02:29.950 --> 00:02:30.783
And,

00:02:32.140 --> 00:02:34.440
but when you go that far

00:02:34.440 --> 00:02:38.000
and then finally learn, it's
already too late, you know

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:41.390
You're going to end up
being a lifer like this.

00:02:41.390 --> 00:02:42.943
- [Interviewer] You were
on the street for how long?

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:45.430
- 76

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.407
to

00:02:48.407 --> 00:02:51.313
2006.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.570
So that's quite a long time, I think.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:55.403
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:02:55.403 --> 00:02:58.273
- And I started getting little rooms but.

00:03:00.501 --> 00:03:01.750
15 by 15

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:02.583
rooms

00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:04.240
with just a,

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:07.160
you know, a bathroom
that's in the hallway.

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:07.993
And,

00:03:07.993 --> 00:03:10.033
but I was too,

00:03:11.190 --> 00:03:12.490
I'm like, you know

00:03:12.490 --> 00:03:15.970
if I'm going to pay to live
in a room because see at first

00:03:15.970 --> 00:03:18.320
I wasn't on SSI and I should have been

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:21.930
on SSI for years before
I ever got onto it.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:22.763
But

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.203
I just,

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.881
just didn't care about anything.

00:03:28.881 --> 00:03:30.113
And,

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.780
I don't know where you
want to go with this

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.298
but I ended up in LA, I was 14.

00:03:37.298 --> 00:03:38.548
That was in 78.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:40.810
And,

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:42.920
being that you do remember.

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:44.500
I don't talk too much about it

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:48.544
but I've had enough of people
who look like they're normal.

00:03:48.544 --> 00:03:51.530
And I was at this place
called Oki Dogs where

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:53.740
there was punk rockers and everything.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:57.720
And I didn't really know
what, what was going on.

00:03:57.720 --> 00:03:59.313
And then one Friday night,

00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:07.960
I got picked up by the LA freeway killer.

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:12.960
And that happened to be a
really bad experience that night

00:04:13.470 --> 00:04:15.410
on and I was on LSD

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:17.773
and

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.240
wherever I jumped out of the car

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:23.210
it was in someplace called Rosemead.

00:04:23.210 --> 00:04:26.940
And to this day, I don't
know where that is, but

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:30.930
or how far it was from
Oki Dogs in Hollywood.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:35.720
But I jumped out of the car,
ran into a, there was a church

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.340
and there was a, in an alley.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.740
And I jumped down in
the window that was like

00:04:39.740 --> 00:04:41.540
in the basement, but it
was like a little spot.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:43.930
And I just stayed there until daylight.

00:04:43.930 --> 00:04:48.180
And some girls, some girl was
going to school and saw me

00:04:49.499 --> 00:04:50.680
and I was bloody and everything.

00:04:50.680 --> 00:04:52.240
And she gave me money.

00:04:52.240 --> 00:04:53.720
And I said, where are you from?

00:04:53.720 --> 00:04:57.070
I said from Hollywood,
you know, and I went back

00:04:57.070 --> 00:05:00.420
to Hollywood and I, that
very day I got a Mohawk

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:03.770
and I wanted to look like the
most scariest evilest thing

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:07.490
because the only people
that seemed like it was cool

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.563
to me were people that looked
like they weren't cool.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:15.920
You know, that was, that's
a different era, you know

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:17.673
than what we see today.

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:20.811
Now, people who look like they ain't cool.

00:05:20.811 --> 00:05:22.080
Aren't cool,

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.900
but that's my own opinion.

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.360
But

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.210
- [Interviewer] So the dad
that raised you was your?

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:30.339
- My stepdad,

00:05:30.339 --> 00:05:31.172
- [Interviewer] Your stepdad.

00:05:31.172 --> 00:05:33.190
- And who I really admire

00:05:33.190 --> 00:05:34.430
and respect.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.640
- [Interviewer] But your,
your, your actual father.

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:38.833
- No, he, I never knew him.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:42.050
- [Interviewer] You don't
know anything of him?

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:46.420
- I knew that he had the
same learning problems, same

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:47.480
like I have a problem

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:51.700
with my back and it's
all pretty much genetic.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:54.050
And I didn't like my posture.

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:57.360
It made me feel like I
couldn't hit on girls.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:01.670
So I really, really was
the only friends that I had

00:06:03.232 --> 00:06:07.700
were basically pets, you
know, rats, particularly

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:10.420
I like rats because they
were the farthest thing

00:06:10.420 --> 00:06:13.180
that any human being really cared about.

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:15.660
But I saw myself in rats.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:17.280
- [Interviewer] Is that the
animal that you relate to?

00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:21.163
Yeah. I still have them to this very day,

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:23.143
but

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:26.470
years later

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:28.470
and like in 88,

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:30.010
87, when they

00:06:30.010 --> 00:06:33.890
they had this big homeless
thing about tent city and SF

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:40.380
and every news camera people
in the world was there filming.

00:06:41.840 --> 00:06:44.020
And I was like, you know

00:06:44.020 --> 00:06:48.210
the way I stand out now is
the way I stood out then.

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:49.760
And they were running to me

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:53.410
and it kind of gave me
a little self-esteem

00:06:53.410 --> 00:06:56.450
about who I am being homeless.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:57.283
You know,

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:00.570
I would hitchhike

00:07:00.570 --> 00:07:03.853
I didn't really go to big
cities because I was scared.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:07.620
And, but I didn't know how

00:07:07.620 --> 00:07:10.940
to survive really well either.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:13.130
I wouldn't carry a
sleeping bag or a blanket

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:16.460
because I didn't want people
to know I was homeless

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:17.820
and

00:07:17.820 --> 00:07:19.090
it was really

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.240
screwed up,

00:07:23.240 --> 00:07:24.160
you know

00:07:24.160 --> 00:07:25.650
and

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:26.840
now that

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:28.160
I am not

00:07:28.160 --> 00:07:29.860
off the street,

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:30.693
but

00:07:31.882 --> 00:07:34.653
and see the effect is
still there, you know?

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:36.563
And,

00:07:38.050 --> 00:07:40.500
and I try real hard to

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.042
turn it off, you know

00:07:42.042 --> 00:07:43.160
and I've been learning a little bit

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:44.433
you know, I'm,

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:46.300
self-taught

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:48.823
I built a computer, I wrote a book.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:53.450
I'm trying to do positive
things, but there's other things

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:54.440
in my life that's

00:07:55.570 --> 00:07:56.403
really,

00:07:59.130 --> 00:08:00.143
it's like a,

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:02.370
it's like,

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:04.090
I'm on hold.

00:08:04.090 --> 00:08:06.550
You know, just like this
thing that's going on

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:10.610
right now with, with
everything being stopped

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:13.673
in the city

00:08:13.673 --> 00:08:18.450
and around the country, that's
the way I feel every day.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:21.060
Anyways, I feel like I'm in a prison.

00:08:21.060 --> 00:08:24.750
As a matter of fact, I've
been to prison and I was freer

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:27.653
on the inside than I have
ever been on the outside.

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:30.773
And I'm

00:08:33.266 --> 00:08:34.099
and I'm

00:08:35.710 --> 00:08:37.560
I'm in pretty solid though.

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:39.880
I've never done anything that I

00:08:39.880 --> 00:08:43.730
for anything that I wouldn't want to do

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:45.303
just so I could get something,

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:48.373
you know.

00:08:50.570 --> 00:08:51.692
- [Interviewer] Are drugs
a part of your life?

00:08:51.692 --> 00:08:52.950
- Yes.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:54.433
I smoke crystal,

00:08:56.550 --> 00:08:58.420
not a lot,

00:08:58.420 --> 00:08:59.320
but at least

00:09:03.660 --> 00:09:05.860
if you were to say, if
you're smoking a cigarette

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:09.830
and you take four or five
hits every day off a cigarette

00:09:09.830 --> 00:09:12.993
and then put it out, that's
about where I'm at now.

00:09:13.914 --> 00:09:15.273
It used to be, I was.

00:09:17.720 --> 00:09:19.110
I started doing

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:25.170
intravenous drugs in 84
when I came up here from LA

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:28.330
because in LA the Olympics was going on.

00:09:28.330 --> 00:09:30.770
The cops was not cool.

00:09:30.770 --> 00:09:34.150
And I came up here and the
scene was really jumping off

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:36.610
and

00:09:36.610 --> 00:09:39.703
I got introduced to a shooting speed.

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:43.100
I was 20 years old and

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:46.943
I never thought

00:09:46.943 --> 00:09:50.760
that I used to tell myself that
I would never going to stay

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:52.520
in this city more than a year

00:09:52.520 --> 00:09:55.250
because I would never leave after that.

00:09:55.250 --> 00:09:56.400
And that I'd never

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:01.950
stay up more than two days.

00:10:01.950 --> 00:10:03.870
And I wouldn't do it more than

00:10:04.800 --> 00:10:05.800
twice a week

00:10:06.650 --> 00:10:08.670
but it ended up being real quick

00:10:08.670 --> 00:10:11.430
like doing it every day, except for two

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:15.220
for months

00:10:16.318 --> 00:10:18.450
And then I, and then
I eventually did leave

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:22.730
and I didn't go through any
culture shock until after 2000.

00:10:22.730 --> 00:10:24.940
I had already been here so many years

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:27.483
that wherever I went after here,

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.370
the world is just so big.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:34.130
And you know, this city,
you can get anything

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:37.320
and do anything within
a three block radius.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:38.720
And

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:40.270
I feel like this is my turf.

00:10:40.270 --> 00:10:41.320
There isn't a person

00:10:41.320 --> 00:10:45.240
in the city that cannot say
they don't know the red man.

00:10:45.240 --> 00:10:49.410
That's what they call
me, red man, you know?

00:10:49.410 --> 00:10:50.243
And,

00:10:52.077 --> 00:10:53.190
and I

00:10:53.190 --> 00:10:54.023
enjoy that

00:10:54.023 --> 00:10:56.000
but I also want to

00:10:57.770 --> 00:10:59.790
also want to get it together.

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:02.370
I don't know what that world is like.

00:11:02.370 --> 00:11:07.137
I mean, I know a lot of good
people, musicians from LA.

00:11:07.137 --> 00:11:10.480
You know Anaheim, you know,

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:12.160
Oxnard area,

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:14.010
Ventura and all of that.

00:11:14.010 --> 00:11:16.698
And, you know, they
support me, but you know

00:11:16.698 --> 00:11:18.738
I'm just a different kind of person

00:11:18.738 --> 00:11:21.060
tired of feeling that way, you know

00:11:23.382 --> 00:11:25.670
- [Interviewer] Did you
always feel like an outcast?

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:27.240
- Yeah. I mean,

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.820
a matter of fact, I even felt like as far

00:11:30.820 --> 00:11:35.820
as hardcore goes like
a biker or punk rocker,

00:11:36.100 --> 00:11:40.100
to me it seems like none
of them has me out beat

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.033
but you know,

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:44.450
when you're 56,

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:45.810
you do think a lot.

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:46.960
And I do think a lot

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:49.920
and I don't discredit

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:51.700
how smart I really am.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:54.760
I would learn a different way, you know

00:11:54.760 --> 00:11:56.390
but it's kinda sucks

00:11:56.390 --> 00:11:57.520
that the way I learned

00:11:58.667 --> 00:12:00.810
it screws me up,

00:12:00.810 --> 00:12:01.643
you know,

00:12:01.643 --> 00:12:06.643
as far as being able to use it,
unless I get lucky, you know

00:12:06.940 --> 00:12:07.840
- [Interviewer] What do
you do for money now?

00:12:07.840 --> 00:12:09.660
How do you support yourself?

00:12:09.660 --> 00:12:12.690
